  message: "Dogfood validation, 2026-05-19 self-analysis. Verdict: moved. Pre-fix claim: 91% collision rate on @dataclass classes (all @dataclass classes in same module collide). Post-fix self-analysis measurement: 4282 Python class nodes, 0 missing stable_id, 3642 unique stable_ids, 811 classes in collision groups, 18.94% overall collision rate. The remaining 18.94% are structurally-identical-but-semantically-distinct test classes — e.g. 49x classes named TestAdaAnalysisUnavailable / TestAsmAnalysisUnavailable / TestCapnpAnalysisUnavailable (per-language fallback tests with identical structure), 36x TestAnalysisRun (literally same name, different modules). These are a different shape of collision (semantic distinctness with no structural signal) — the @dataclass bug from the original claim is fully resolved. Verification script: /tmp/inv-validation/verify_dogfood.py. Following up: structurally-identical-but-different-modules class collision could be filed as a separate item if desired, but isn't the original INV-fusus bug."  # 0323
